Fri Oct 30 11:29:45 UTC 2026 - Tina Müller <timueller+perl@suse.de>

- updated to 0.200.0 (0.20)
   see /usr/share/doc/packages/perl-Spreadsheet-XLSX/Changes

  0.20  2026-10-29
      - Security: limit ZIP entry counts and uncompressed sizes; read members
        incrementally and reject inconsistent size metadata.
      - Security: validate number format IDs and escape regex lookups to prevent
        regex injection from crafted styles.
      - Security: reject out-of-range date values to prevent excessive CPU usage.
      - Security: validate cell references against XLSX worksheet limits before
        indexing cell arrays, preventing excessive allocation from invalid rows.
      - Add cpanfile for easy dependency installation.
      - Improve Readme.
  0.19  2026-10-29
      - Security: replace string eval of number-format conditions with strict
        numeric comparisons; invalid conditions use the fallback format section.
        CVE-2026-115943 bsc#1288922
        Prevents arbitrary Perl code execution when parsing crafted XLSX files.
      - Add regression tests for numeric conditions and malicious XLSX formats.

